# Every text file is checked out with LF, on every system (D101). A shell script with CRLF endings does not run in Git Bash on a
# Windows runner, and the golden files and fixtures of the tests are compared byte for byte. The one exception is a Windows batch
# file, which belongs to Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.whl binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite3 binary
